root@74feeeadfed3:/home/travis/build/failed/google/auto# cat > ../failed_reasons.txt <<EOF
> The build fails because the modules (common, factory, service, value) are inheriting from 'auto-parent' version 3, which seems to have a dependency on 'tools.jar' at a system path that does not exist in the current Java 11 environment. The error message explicitly states it cannot find 'tools.jar' at '/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64/../lib/tools.jar'.
> 
> The project root contains a newer 'auto-parent' version 4-SNAPSHOT which is being built but not used by the modules. This newer parent likely has better handling for tools.jar or can be modified.
> 
> Plan:
> 1. Update 'common/pom.xml', 'factory/pom.xml', 'service/pom.xml', and 'value/pom.xml' to inherit from 'auto-parent' version 4-SNAPSHOT.
> 2. Add <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath> to the parent declaration in these files so they find the local parent.
> EOF
